// CF-2: a negated guard flips the KIL's condition-code TEST, and does not
// invert the comparison.
//
// The reference emits SGT (not SLE) and predicates the kill on EQ instead
// of NE.  A lowering that inverted the comparison instead would produce
// the same pixels for `>` but not for `==` or a NaN operand, and would be
// a different container - so the assertion is on the opcode AND the test.
//
// Second measured effect, asserted here too: a negated LONE comparison
// loses the fx12 demotion (fp32), while a negated CHAIN keeps it.
void main(float4 c : TEXCOORD0, out float4 o : COLOR)
{
    if (!(c.a > 0.5)) discard;
    o = c;
}
